    "ver": "0.37.0"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 2 / 2: Fit a track to a character -> SCAIL cylinder pose video (once per character)\n\n1. **Load Skeleton Track**: the folder workflow 1 printed, e.g. `pss_tracks/sprint_kicks_v1` (looked up in `ComfyUI/input/`, then `ComfyUI/output/`).\n2. **Load Image**: your character, side view, facing right, whole body, on white. The example uses `cop_on_white.png` from the Posed Sprite Sheet Generator V2 bundle.\n3. **DWPose Estimator** (comfyui_controlnet_aux): the character's keypoints; the fit takes its bone lengths from them.\n4. **Fit Track to Character**: every bone keeps its direction per frame and takes the character's length. *canvas* = width (height 1024 + *pad_top*), *hip_x* = where the hips stay, *fixed_shift* = one shift for the whole clip (walks). Check *Fit check*.\n**Preview Skeleton Track** plays the fitted poses (the character's proportions) inside the node.\n5. **Render SCAIL Cylinders**: the pose video SCAIL-Preview takes (mp4 + PNG frames), z-buffered so the near limbs stay in front.\n\nSame track, another character: change only the picture and run again."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
